<title>BELGIUM: EU says sets 15 Ecus/T semolina export tax.</title>
<headline>EU says sets 15 Ecus/T semolina export tax.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday said it set a tax of 15 Ecus a tonne on daily exports of durum wheat semolina, a European Commission spokesman said.</p>
<p>France's grain office ONIC earlier reported that a tax of 20 Ecus a tonne had been agreed.</p>
<p>The tax, which comes into force on publication in the EU Official Journal, replaces a nil value refund.</p>
</text>
